{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git status --short --branch; sed -n '1,160p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; sed -n '590,685p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc; rg -n 'stream/(append|next|cursor)|require\\\\)|link-request|:make-stream' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr test/yang/php/antlr | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"## eval-bridge...origin/eval-bridge\n?? collab/yang-php/1794624900000-engineer-eval-bridge-r16-resume.prompt.md\n?? collab/yang-php/1794624900000-engineer-eval-bridge-r16.gpt-6.1-terra.stdout.log\n(ns yang.php.antlr.lower\n  \"The PHP lowering interpreter: CST packets in, Universal AST program\n   batches out (docs/design/yang.php.md sections 3, 7). Portable.\n\n   Per packet: validate the tree, analyze scopes (`yang.php.antlr.scope`),\n   then lower with one `case` arm per grammar rule. A rule P1 does not lower\n   fails with `:yang.php/unsupported` naming the rule and construct; a rule\n   with no arm fails with `:yang.php/unhandled-rule`. Nothing is silently\n   dropped.\n\n   Decided lowering rules (collab/1792905000000 plan):\n   - A top-level `$x` is `(php/global-get \\\"x\\\")` / `(php/global-set! \\\"x\\\" v)`;\n     inside a function it is a lexical cell `$x` allocated at entry holding\n     `:php/undef`. Loops are self-applied `:loop`-marked lambdas whose\n     `break`/`continue` are `php/call-ec` escapes bound to `%brk<id>` and\n     `%cont<id>`, created only when the body uses them; the `:loops` stack of\n     the context resolves `break n`. `switch` is one stack level: a chain of\n     lambdas whose bodies tail-call the next case.\n   - A function is `(php/declare-function! name (php/make-function name spec\n     (fn [%fn %args] body) statics))`; top-level unconditional declarations\n     are hoisted. `return` is an escape from `php/call-ec`, bound only when\n     the body has a `return`.\n   - The unit is its hoisted top-level function declarations, then its\n     statements in order, run under `php/run-main`.\n   - Inline HTML is `(php/echo \\\"bytes\\\")`; `echo a, b` is\n     `(php/echo (php/to-string a))` per operand; a PHP string is a byte\n     carrier (a latin-1 string), literal text resolved here to UTF-8 bytes.\n   - `&&`, `||`, `and`, `or`, `?:` are `:if` nodes over `php/to-bool`, never\n     applications, so they short circuit. Every other operator is one\n     application of a `php/` function of the prelude.\n   - A call `f(a, b)` resolves `f` before any argument runs:\n     `(let [%f (php/resolve-fn \\\"f\\\" \\\"F\\\")] (php/call %f [a b]))`.\n   - Generated names are `%<prefix><cst-id>`; `%` cannot begin a PHP name, so\n     no guest name shadows a name the lowering emits. The lowering never\n     names a runtime key (`php.rt/*`).\n\n   Diagnostic namespace: \\\"yang.php\\\".\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [dao.host.text :as text]\n    [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as p]\n    [yang.core.lower :as core]\n    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    [yang.core.prelude :as core-prelude]\n    [yang.core.stage :as core-stage]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.builtins :as builtins]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.php.antlr.scope :as scope]\n    [yang.stage :as stage]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Diagnostics\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private diagnostic-ns \"yang.php\")\n\n\n(defn- unsupported!\n  [n construct]\n  (core/unsupported! diagnostic-ns \"PHP\" n construct))\n\n\n(defn- compile-error!\n  \"A PHP compile-time error: the program is refused, never run.\"\n  [n message]\n  (throw (ex-info message\n                  {:yang.php/diagnostic :yang.php/compile-error,\n                   :rule (:rule n),\n                   :span (:span n)})))\n\n\n(defn- warn!\n  \"Record a warning-severity lowering diagnostic: the program still lowers.\"\n  [ctx n kind message data]\n  (swap! (:warnings ctx)\n         conj\n         (merge {:yang.php/diagnostic kind,\n                 :severity :warning,\n                 :message message,\n                 :span (:span n)}\n                data)))\n\n\n(def unsupported-rules\n  \"Grammar rules P1 does not lower, with the construct each names.\"\n  {\"gotoStatement\" :goto,\n   \"declareStatement\" :declare,\n   \"importStatement\" :import,\n   \"newExpr\" :new,\n   \"yieldExpression\" :yield,\n   \"scriptText\" :inline-script,\n   \"classConstant\" :class-constant})\n\n\n(def ^:private prefix-refusals\n  \"Expression forms led by a keyword or operator token.\"\n  {\"Clone\" :clone,\n   \"New\" :new,\n   \"Eval\" :eval,\n   \"Include\" :include,\n   \"IncludeOnce\" :include,\n   \"Require\" :include,\n   \"RequireOnce\" :include,\n   \"Yield\" :yield,\n   \"List\" :list})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Unit paths and linker names (plan P6 R2/R3)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private unit-path-chars #\"[A-Za-z0-9_\\-./]*\")\n\n\n(defn normalize-unit-path\n  \"`{:path p}` for the relative path `s` normalized (segments joined by `/`,\n   `.` and empty segments dropped, `..` collapsed), else `{:error e}`:\n   `:unit-path` for a character outside `[A-Za-z0-9_\\\\-./]`, `:include-path`\n   for an absolute path or one escaping the composition root.\"\n  [s]\n  (cond\n    (not (re-matches unit-path-chars s)) {:error :unit-path}\n    (str/starts-with? s \"/\") {:error :include-path}\n    :else (let [segs (reduce (fn [acc seg]\n                               (cond\n                                 (or (= seg \"\") (= seg \".\")) acc\n                                 (= seg \"..\") (if (empty? acc) (reduced nil) (pop acc))\n                                 :else (conj acc seg)))\n                             []\n                             (str/split s #\"/\"))]\n            (if (or (nil? segs) (empty? segs))\n              {:error :include-path}\n              {:path (str/join \"/\" segs)}))))\n\n\n(defn path-module-symbol\n  \"The linker module of unit path `path`: `phpm.` then the path with `/` as\n   `$` and `.` as `$$`, nothing dropped (injective: plan P6 R2).\"\n  [path]\n  (symbol (str \"phpm.\" (str/replace (str/replace path \"/\" \"$\") \".\" \"$$\"))))\n\n\n(def classmap-name\n  \"The unit name of the autoload class map; a unit path cannot begin with\n   `$`, so no unit collides with it.\"\n  \"$classmap\")\n\n\n(def classmap-module\n  \"The linker module of the class map.\"\n  (path-module-symbol classmap-name))\n\n\n(defn- path-dirname\n(defn- bare\n  [name]\n  (subs name 1))\n\n\n(defn- checked-var\n  \"`name`; `$this` is read through the running method's function cell.\"\n  [_n name]\n  name)\n\n\n(defn- cc-node\n  \"The calling class: the method's lexical `%cc`, null outside a class.\"\n  [ctx]\n  (if (:cc ctx) (u/v '%cc) (u/lit :php/null)))\n\n\n(defn- this-var?\n  [name]\n  (= \"$this\" name))\n\n\n(defn- this-node\n  [ctx]\n  (cond\n    (:fn ctx) (app* 'php/this-of (u/v '%fn))\n    (:module? ctx) (app* 'php/ctx-this (u/v '%ctx))\n    :else (app* 'php/throw-error (u/lit \"Error\") (u/lit \"Using $this when not in object context\"))))\n\n\n(declare chain-calls member-vis class-ref-node class-name-node leftmost-token-text lower-class lower-new\n         lower-class-constant lower-initializer-part class-spec*)\n\n\n(defn- static-var?\n  \"A static property is a variable named `::Class::prop`.\"\n  [name]\n  (str/starts-with? name \"::\"))\n\n\n(defn- static-parts\n  [name]\n  (let [[_ cls prop] (str/split name #\"::\")]\n    [cls prop]))\n\n\n(defn- cv-node\n  \"The holder cell node of variable `name` in the current scope, or nil for a\n   global.\"\n  [ctx name]\n  (cond\n    (static-var? name)\n    (let [[cls prop] (static-parts name)]\n      (app* 'php/sprop-cell (class-ref-node ctx nil cls) (u/lit prop) (cc-node ctx)))\n    (:fn ctx) (u/v (symbol name))\n    :else nil))\n\n\n(defn- display-name\n  [name]\n  (if (static-var? name) (second (static-parts name)) (bare name)))\n\n\n(defn- scope-op\n  \"The operation `op` (`get`, `set!`, ...) on a top-level variable: the\n   globals of the entry unit, or the including scope `%scope` inside an\n   included unit's body (plan P6 R5).\"\n  [ctx op name & more]\n  (if (:module? ctx)\n    (apply app* (symbol \"php\" (str \"dict-\" op)) (u/v '%scope) (u/lit (bare name)) more)\n    (apply app* (symbol \"php\" (str \"global-\" op)) (u/lit (bare name)) more)))\n\n\n(defn- dynamic-var?\n  [name]\n  (and (map? name) (contains? name :dynamic-name)))\n\n\n(defn- dynamic-scope-node\n  [ctx]\n  (if (or (:fn ctx) (:module? ctx)) (u/v '%scope) (u/lit :php/globals)))\n\n\n(defn- dynamic-op\n  [ctx op name & more]\n  (apply app* (symbol \"php\" (str \"dict-\" op)) (dynamic-scope-node ctx)\n         (app* 'php/to-string (:dynamic-name name)) more))\n\n\n(defn- read-var\n  [ctx name]\n  (cond\n    (dynamic-var? name) (dynamic-op ctx \"get\" name)\n    (= \"$GLOBALS\" name) (app* 'php/globals-read)\n    (this-var? name) (this-node ctx)\n    :else (if-let [cv (cv-node ctx name)]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:111:  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\ntest/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc:116:   :link-request (:requests pair),\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:41:         cursor (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor requests stream/anchor-oldest))]\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:51:  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\ntest/yang/php/antlr/e2e_harness.clj:79:     (stream/append! cst-log (cst/parse-source source))\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_service_test.clj:23:        start (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor requests stream/anchor-oldest))\ntest/yang/php/antlr/eval_service_test.clj:24:        response-start (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cur