{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '80,120p;480,535p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; rg -n 'defn context|defn lower-program|:linked\\\\?|request-node|defn- unit-node|defn- call-node|safepoint' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/lower.cljc | tail -45; rg -n 'link-format|ast-contract|walker|:ast' src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc | tail -30\"","aggregated_output":"    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]\n    [yang.core.prelude :as core]\n    [yang.core.call :as call]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.builtins :as builtins]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude-module :as module-defs]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude-p9 :as p9-defs]\n    [yang.php.antlr.quoted :refer [defquoted]]\n    [yin.vm.integer :as integer]))\n\n\n(def host-names\n  \"Module exports the prelude calls. The two `dsg__` doors are the VM\n   provenance primitive's reserved mint and reader (yin.vm.module: guest\n   code may neither spell nor construct their names); the php module\n   declares them the way python's adoption did — §8.10.7 wrapper retention\n   mints and authenticates through them, never through prelude code.\"\n  (into '#{cell/new cell/get cell/set! cell/dsg__new-provenance cell/dsg__provenance\n           data/count data/nth data/subvec data/str-concat\n           data/str-length data/str-join data/str-compare data/str->code-points\n           data/code-points->str data/substring data/float64 data/float-value\n           data/content= data/dissoc data/into\n           integer/integer? integer/add integer/sub integer/neg integer/mul integer/compare\n           integer/to-float integer/compare-float integer/true-div integer/pow\n           integer/shift-left integer/shift-right integer/bit-and integer/bit-or\n           integer/bit-xor integer/bit-not integer/from-float integer/quot-rem\n           integer/floor-div-mod integer/format integer/parse\n           integer/float-digits integer/decimal->float\n           stream/put! stream/cursor stream/poll!}\n        call/host-names))\n\n\n(defquoted ^:private core-definitions\n  \"Pure definitions: lambdas only, so defining them runs nothing.\"\n  '[;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- basics\n    [php/vconj (fn [xs x] (conj xs x))]\n    [php/pair (fn [a b] (php/vconj (php/vconj [] a) b))]\n    [php/f (fn [h] (data/float64 h))]\n    [php/h (fn [x] (data/float-value x))]\n    [php/inf (fn [] (data/float-value ##Inf))]\n             files (php/request-field request :php.request/files)\n             req (php/request-merge-into geta post)]\n         (do (cell/set! php.rt/request request)\n             (php/global-put! \"_GET\" geta)\n             (php/global-put! \"_POST\" post)\n             (php/global-put! \"_COOKIE\" cookies)\n             (php/global-put! \"_SERVER\" server)\n             (php/global-put! \"_ENV\" env)\n             (php/global-put! \"_FILES\" files)\n             (php/global-put! \"_REQUEST\" req)\n             :php/null)))]\n    [php/resolve-request\n     ;; the request record `run-main` binds: a plain record binds directly,\n     ;; while a composition-supplied request-stream reference is consumed\n     ;; here at runtime (one record, oldest first) — the stream, never the\n     ;; record, is what the harness composes into the program, so request\n     ;; data never travels as compiled UAST content. An empty stream keeps\n     ;; the empty defaults.\n     (fn [request]\n       (if (if (nil? request) true (= request :php/null))\n         :php/null\n         (if (= (get request :type) :stream-ref)\n           (let [v (stream/poll! (stream/cursor request))]\n             (if (= v :dao.stream/blocked) :php/null v))\n           request)))]\n    [php/emit-response!\n     ;; the task's response emission: onto the composition-supplied\n     ;; response stream DURING execution when run-main received one, else\n     ;; onto the response cell (compositions without streams).\n     (fn [record]\n       (let [h (cell/get php.rt/response-stream)]\n         (if (= h :php/null)\n           (cell/set! php.rt/response (php/vconj (cell/get php.rt/response) record))\n           (do (stream/put! h record) :php/null))))]\n    [php/drain-loop\n     ;; poll `cur` to `:dao.stream/blocked`, accumulating the records in\n     ;; stream order; the composition drains what execution emitted.\n     (fn [cur acc]\n       (let [v (stream/poll! cur)]\n         (if (= v :dao.stream/blocked)\n           acc\n           (php/drain-loop cur (php/vconj acc v)))))]\n    [php/drain-stream\n     ;; every record execution emitted on the composition-supplied stream\n     ;; `ref`, oldest first.\n     (fn [ref]\n       (php/drain-loop (stream/cursor ref) []))]\n    [php/echo\n     (fn [s]\n       (let [bufs (cell/get php.rt/out)\n             i (- (data/count bufs) 1)]\n         (do (if (if (= i 0) (> (data/str-length s) 0) false)\n               (cell/set! php.rt/headers-sent true)\n               :php/null)\n             (cell/set! php.rt/out (assoc bufs i (conj (get bufs i) s))))))]\n    [php/bi-ob-start\n1275:  (when-not (:linked? ctx) (unsupported! n :include))\n1640:(defn- call-node\n3703:              :linked? (boolean linked?),\n3783:(defn- unit-node\n3823:   variable scope, method context and safepoint hooks. It does not initialize\n3827:   (let [ctx (assoc (context packet {:path (or path entry-path) :linked? true})\n3863:   (`:request-node`, an opaque UAST node) at the composition level — the\n3865:  [:prelude :path :paths :class-map :request-node :response-node :diag-node])\n3878:(defn lower-program\n3892:   (plan P6 R9), which takes the place of `:paths`; `:request-node` is the\n3901:  ([packet {:keys [prelude paths path class-map request-node response-node diag-node],\n3909:         request-node (or request-node (u/sexp->uast :php/null))\n3910:         ctx (context packet {:path (or path entry-path), :linked? linked?})\n3919:                (app* 'php/run-main (u/lam [] (unit-node ctx)) request-node\n3922:                (app* 'php/run-main (u/lam [] (unit-node ctx)) request-node))]\n3961:  (let [ctx (context packet {:path path, :linked? true})]\n3986:  (let [ctx (assoc (context packet {:path path, :linked? true}) :module? true)\n4104:                          (let [ctx (context packet {:path name, :linked? true})]\n481:  (link-format\n672:            {:keys [format contract]} (link-format state)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
