{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'IModuleKernel|link-format' src/cljc/yin/vm | head -50; cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/safepoint.cljc | head -65; sed -n '6190,6240p' src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/prelude.cljc; sed -n '1,120p' src/cljc/yang/safepoint.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:1206:  module/IModuleKernel\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:1207:  (link-format [_] {:format :yin.ast/code, :contract vm/ast-contract})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:440:  module/IModuleKernel\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:441:  (link-format [_]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:952:  module/IModuleKernel\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc:953:  (link-format [_] {:format format-tag, :contract vm/stack-contract})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:476:(defprotocol IModuleKernel\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:481:  (link-format\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:672:            {:keys [format contract]} (link-format state)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:895:  module/IModuleKernel\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/register.cljc:896:  (link-format [_] {:format format-tag, :contract vm/register-contract})\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2559:  (let [children-of (if (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2607:  (let [kernel (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel vm)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:682:- **Roots:** the kernel's registers (`IModuleKernel/gc-roots`), the store and every module store, `:parked`, `:wait-set`, `:ready-queue`, the value being boxed, and every pinned cell. Code, images, the registry, primitives and `:resources` are not roots.\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc:309:  (let [f (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel k) (:format (module/link-format k)))]\n(ns yang.php.antlr.safepoint\n  \"The PHP `:loop` and `:call` hooks. A bounded run charges one safepoint to\n   its per-run counter; exhaustion unwinds past guest handlers and raises the\n   operational fatal, not a guest Throwable.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.core.module :as module]))\n\n\n(def profile\n  {:loop 'php.sp/loop, :call {:hook 'php.sp/call, :sequence true}})\n\n\n(def ticks-profile\n  \"Statement completion hooks for PHP's lexical ticks directives. This is\n   separate from the execution-budget profile so ticks do not charge it.\"\n  {:line {:hook 'php.sp/line, :operands true, :after true}})\n\n\n(def fatal-text\n  \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\")\n\n\n(def ^:private function-definitions\n  '[[php.sp/exhaust!\n     ;; the terminal root escape: guest handlers, returns and finalizers\n     ;; cannot replace the operational fatal\n     (fn []\n       (php/root-fatal \"Maximum execution time of 30 seconds exceeded\"))]\n    [php.sp/tick\n     (fn []\n       (let [n (cell/get php.sp/remaining)]\n         (if (= n 0)\n           (php.sp/exhaust!)\n           (do (cell/set! php.sp/remaining (- n 1)) :php/null))))]\n    [php.sp/loop (fn [] (php.sp/tick))]\n    [php.sp/call (fn [] (php.sp/tick))]])\n\n\n(defn- definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n\n\n(defn program\n  \"The bounded run: hook definitions and a counter holding `budget`, then the\n   safepoint-derived program `ast`. `budget` must be a non-negative integer;\n   anything else is a named host-side error, not a guest diagnostic.\"\n  [budget ast]\n  (when-not (and (integer? budget) (not (neg? budget)))\n    (throw (ex-info \"php.sp/remaining budget must be a non-negative integer\"\n                    {:yang.php.antlr.safepoint/error :invalid-budget\n                     :budget budget})))\n  (u/mark-tails\n    (u/then (definitions->uast function-definitions)\n            (u/then (u/def! 'php.sp/remaining (u/sexp->uast (list 'cell/new budget)))\n                    ast))))\n\n\n(defn module-spec\n  \"The linked ticks hook delegates to the shared PHP runtime.\"\n  [registry php-address]\n  (let [ast (module/module-tree\n              [(module/require-node 'php)\n               (u/def! 'line (u/sexp->uast '(fn [line site] (php/tick-line line site))))])\n                       (mapv (fn [[nm sym]] (list 'php/register! nm sym))\n                             builtins))]\n                ;; last, so a failed init never reports ready\n                [(define 'php.rt/state :php/ready) :php/null])\n              :php/null)))\n\n\n(def definitions\n  \"The single definition list, `[store-key form]` in definition order: every\n   prelude function, the literal state slot, then `php/init!`. Defining them\n   runs nothing.\"\n  (into (into (into core-definitions module-defs/definitions) p9-defs/definitions)\n        [['php.rt/state :php/uninit]\n         ['php/init! (init-form)]]))\n\n\n(defn- definitions->uast\n  [defs]\n  ;; A linear `then` chain adds two tree levels per definition; at this\n  ;; prelude's size the bundled tree runs ~900 deep and overflows the Dart\n  ;; stack in the recursive tree walkers. Balance the sequence, preserving\n  ;; left-to-right effects and the last definition's value.\n  (letfn [(sequence-tree\n            [nodes]\n            (if (<= (count nodes) 1)\n              (first nodes)\n              (let [middle (quot (count nodes) 2)]\n                (u/then (sequence-tree (subvec nodes 0 middle))\n                        (sequence-tree (subvec nodes middle))))))]\n    (sequence-tree (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs))))\n\n\n(def functions-uast\n  \"The bundled shared-call definitions, PHP lambdas and literal state slot.\"\n  (definitions->uast (into call/definitions definitions)))\n\n\n(def uast\n  \"The bundled prelude: every definition, then the task's runtime state\n   allocated by `php/init!`.\"\n  (u/then functions-uast (u/sexp->uast '(php/init!))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The module emitter: the same definition list as the linker module `php`\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def module-name\n  \"The linker module the PHP runtime profile is published as.\"\n  'php)\n\n(ns yang.safepoint\n  \"The safepoint stage (Architect safepoint-interpreter design, slice 1): a\n   pure rewrite of a canonical program tree `A` into a derived tree `A'` that\n   applies a hook at every frontend-marked site the profile maps.\n   Language-neutral: it knows the Universal AST row grammar and the\n   frontend-metadata side table, nothing about any guest language. The hooks'\n   meaning lives in a per-language hook prelude; the evaluator never learns\n   what a safepoint is.\n\n   - A site is a `:lambda` occurrence the frontend marked with `:yang/site`\n     metadata, which projection puts in the side table as\n     `[origin root path :yang/site kind]`. A profile `{kind hook-symbol}`\n     selects sites; a kind it omits is not inserted.\n   - Insertion prefixes the site's body with an ordinary `:application` of\n     the hook, sequenced through a lambda whose one binder is `binder`, in a\n     reserved namespace: no new tag, no gensym counter. An exit kind\n     (`exit-kinds`: `:return` at `:call` sites) wraps the body instead: its\n     hook is applied to the body's value, so it runs on normal exit only.\n   - A mark's value is a kind, or a vector `[kind datum ...]`: the data\n     (a function's name and line, a statement's line) are literals the\n     frontend knows and the derived tree may need. A profile entry is a\n     hook symbol, or `{:hook symbol :operands true}` to apply the hook to\n     the mark's data. A statement kind (`statement-kinds`: `:line`) marks\n     any node, not a lambda; its hook is applied before the node, which\n     is sequenced after it.\n   - Every tail mark is stripped and recomputed over the whole derived tree\n     (`yang.tails`): a wrapped body's old tail calls would otherwise skip\n     its wrapper. With no site selected `A'` is `A`, row for row.\n   - `A` is never modified. Names, the ledger and publication refer to it;\n     the link is a `:derive` record with input `A`, output `A'`, function\n     `function`, and a profile pinning the hook map and the address of the\n     sorted site set. Insertion is deterministic, so a repeat writes the\n     same record.\n   - `A'` leaves on the stage's own medium in a projected envelope whose\n     batch token is the record's address, so its occurrence origin is an\n     ordinary `[:source medium' token 0]`. No side table is copied: an `A'`\n     node's facts are a join back to `A` through the site set. The one\n     exception is the C1 claim: when the input claims `:yang/call-site`\n     coverage, `derive-envelope` recomputes its rows over `A'` (never\n     copies them — paths shift) and records the input→output occurrence\n     correspondence as data.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    [yang.stage :as stage]\n    [yang.tails :as tails]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n\n\n(def binder\n  \"The parameter of every inserted sequencing lambda.\"\n  'yang.safepoint/_)\n\n\n(def result-binder\n  \"The value preserved by an after-hook.\"\n  'yang.safepoint/value)\n\n\n(def function\n  \"The `:yin.ledger/function` of a safepoint derivation.\"\n  :yang.safepoint/insert)\n\n\n(def site-key\n  \"The frontend-metadata key a site mark travels under.\"\n  :yang/site)\n\n\n(def call-site-key\n  \"The frontend-metadata key of the call-site occurrence contract C1,\n   recomputed over a derived tree beside the safepoint site marks.\"\n  :yang/call-site)\n\n\n(defn sites\n  \"`{path mark}` (a kind, or `[kind datum ...]`) of every site marked in the frontend-metadata relation\n   `metadata` at occurrence `origin` of tree `root`.\"\n  [metadata origin root]\n  (into {}\n        (keep (fn [[o r path k v]]\n                (when (and (= o origin) (= r root) (= k site-key))\n                  [path v])))\n        metadata))\n\n\n(defn site-set\n  \"The selected sites as a sorted vector of `[path mark]`, a mark a kind or `[kind datum ...]`, in an order every\n   host computes alike.\"\n  [selected]\n  (vec (sort-by pr-str (map vec selected))))\n\n\n(def exit-kinds\n  \"Exit kind -> the entry kind whose sites it wraps. An exit hook is applied\n   to the value of the site's body, so it runs after a normal exit and its\n   answer is the body's value; an escape out of the body skips it.\"\n  {:return :call})\n\n\n(def statement-kinds\n  \"Kinds whose sites are any node, not a lambda: the hook runs before the\n   node, and the node's value is the site's.\"\n  #{:line})\n\n\n(defn- mark-kind\n  [mark]\n  (if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark))\n\n\n(defn- entry-hook\n  \"The `{:hook sym :operands [literal ...]}` of profile entry `entry` at a\n   site marked `mark`, or nil.\"\n  [entry mark]\n  (when entry\n    (if (map? entry)\n      {:hook (:hook entry),\n       :operands (when (:operands entry) (vec (rest mark)))}\n      {:hook entry})))\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
